  alt="Windows applications shown as native Linux windows"
>
  <h2>Windows apps, without the Windows desktop</h2>
  <p>Regulus keeps a Windows machine running off to the side and streams each app straight to your desktop over RDP RemoteApp. Word, Explorer, or that one internal tool you're stuck with all open as normal windows, sitting next to your Linux apps.</p>
  <p>You won't get a second monitor, or a Windows desktop crammed into a window. You just get the apps, along with a shared clipboard and working sound.</p>
</Split>
